Subject: [PATCH 10388/11362] Root-cause exp6753: it checkpoints into a
 TemporaryDirectory

Three attempts have burned hours on the object-table A/B for nothing. Measured on
the 11h29m run before killing it: 39,732 CPU-seconds, 490 completed generations,
14,911 timing lines, ZERO errors -- and no artifact. It was never stuck; it ground
steadily for eleven hours and left nothing.

The cause is one line (experiment_6753...py:1207):

    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="carnot-exp6753-") as temp_dir:

The worker DOES checkpoint after every row into a path under that tree, and the
context manager deletes the tree on exit. So it checkpoints diligently and then
guarantees the checkpoints are destroyed unless the parent reaches aggregation.
Any kill, cap or crash vaporises every completed row.

That also explains the conductor's v2 hitting the 4,803s codex cap twice: the
plan is 20 games x 3 seeds x 2 arms x 2 models, all-or-nothing, at ~85s per
generation. The cap is a symptom of the structure, not an independent failure.

Recorded with it: while running it held 17,884 MiB on GPU 0 and the V590
capstone's exclusive_gpu_without_unrelated_compute gate named pid 3306606
explicitly, memory_free_mb 5969 against 22,610 required. That is a gate quoting my
process id -- evidence, not the correlation I got wrong yesterday. GPU 0 returned
to 24,120 MiB free on kill.

The fix is small: a durable checkpoint path keyed by model + plan hash, with the
worker resuming from it. Today's 490 generations would have counted. The entry
says explicitly not to re-run as-is, because a fourth attempt with the same
structure produces the same nothing.

